    "I_sample13": {
        "body": "## Team accounts\n\nA workspace has one **owner**. This build adds the owner table, sign-in sessions and the settings page.\n\n- [x] Owner table and sign-up\n- [ ] Sign-in sessions\n- [ ] Owner settings page\n\n| Column | Type | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `id` | uuid | primary key |\n| `email` | text | unique, lower-cased before it is stored and compared by the database |\n| `created_at` | timestamptz | set by the server |\n\n```ts\nexport async function createOwner(email: string, passwordHash: string): Promise<Owner> {\n  return db.insert(owners).values({ email: email.toLowerCase(), passwordHash }).returning().then(([row]) => row!);\n}\n```\n\n<details><summary>Open questions</summary>\n\nShould an owner be able to invite a second owner? See [#200](https://github.com/acme/api/issues/200).\n\n</details>\n\n![Sign-up flow](https://example.com/sign-up-flow.png)\n",
        "format": "markdown",
        "author": "maddec01",
        "assignees": ["maddec01", "claude-bot"],
        "createdAt": "2026-10-12T09:14:00Z",
        "milestone": "Cloud v0.1",
